<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00H4">Remark <span data-tag="00H4">1.2.3.17</span>.</a> The functor $\pi _0: \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}\rightarrow \operatorname{Set}$ of Corollary <a data-tag="00GS" href="/tag/00GS">1.2.1.21</a> can be regarded as special case of Proposition <a data-tag="002F" href="/tag/002F">1.2.3.15</a>: it agrees with the functor $| \bullet |^{Q}$, where $Q^{\bullet }: \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}\rightarrow \operatorname{Set}$ is a constant functor whose value is a singleton set $\ast \in \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}$ (see Proposition <a data-tag="00GQ" href="/tag/00GQ">1.2.1.19</a>). </p>
